      "id": "AUTH-001",
      "title": "validateHandlerOrder bypasses max pricing bound when computeRatioX96 returns zero sentinel",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence_score": 85,
      "confidence_deductions": [
        {
          "reason": "Requires token creator to set only max bound (no min bound)",
          "deduction": -10
        },
        {
          "reason": "Bounded non-compounding impact (single order bypass)",
          "deduction": -5
        }
      ],
      "status": "confirmed",
      "source_hypothesis": "H-R5-CH-02",
      "category": "access-control",
      "description": "AMMStandardHook.validateHandlerOrder does not check for sqrtPriceX96 == 0 (overflow sentinel from SqrtPriceCalculator.computeRatioX96). When a CLOB order has amounts causing uint160 overflow (e.g., amount0=1, amount1=type(uint256).max), computeRatioX96 returns 0. The max bound check evaluates 0 > maxSqrtPriceX96 which is always false, bypassing the bound entirely. By contrast, _validatePricingBounds (used in beforeSwap/afterSwap) correctly checks sqrtPriceX96 == 0 at line 847-850 and reverts with InvalidPrice.",
      "impact": "Token creator who sets only a max price bound (minSqrtPriceX96=0) to prevent manipulative high-price CLOB orders has their protection silently bypassed. An attacker can place CLOB orders at any effective price above the max bound.",
      "proof_sketch": "test_H02_bypassWithRealisticMaxBound: Sets max bound to Q96 (1:1 price), then calls validateHandlerOrder with amounts causing overflow. Function does NOT revert, proving the max bound is bypassed.",
      "victim": "Token creator who sets max pricing bounds on CLOB orders",
      "extractable_value": "Depends on token pair liquidity. The attacker can place orders at prices exceeding the creator's max bound, potentially manipulating the effective price of CLOB fills.",
      "attack_sequence": [
        "1. Token creator sets pricing bounds on their token: minSqrtPriceX96=0, maxSqrtPriceX96=Q96",
        "2. Attacker calls CLOB openOrder with extreme amounts (amount0=1, amount1=type(uint256).max)",
        "3. validateHandlerOrder computes sqrtPriceX96 via computeRatioX96, which overflows and returns 0",
        "4. Max bound check: 0 > Q96 is FALSE, so the order passes validation",
        "5. Order sits in the CLOB at an effectively unconstrained price"
      ],
      "test_file": "lbamm-hooks-and-handlers/test/AuditAuthForgerW1.t.sol",
      "test_passes": true,
      "prerequisites": [
        "Token creator must set only max bound (min=0)",
        "CLOB order book exists for the token pair"
      ],
      "repos": [
        "lbamm-hooks-and-handlers"
      ],
